+---
+name: subscription-harness-order
+description: Prefer Claude, then Cursor, for work assigned across existing subscriptions
+alwaysApply: true
+---
+
+# Subscription Harness Order
+
+When assigning work across Claude and Cursor using existing subscriptions, use Claude first while its access remains authorized and available. This preference governs that choice; it does not require delegating ordinary work from another harness.
+
+If Claude returns an actual usage-limit response, preserve its exact public limit/reset message and a checked checkpoint of completed work, useful outputs, the pending step, and existing holds. Continue in Cursor so it can finish, reusing completed work without duplicate inference. Do not infer a quota block from percentages or slowness.
+
+Preserve existing authorization, privacy boundaries, holds, spending limits, and cancellation or expiry boundaries. Switching harnesses does not authorize renewal, extra credits, overages, direct paid provider APIs, or bypassing quota or security controls. If no authorized harness is available, retain the checkpoint and report the remaining work.
